From: WorkBuddy <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: emit the YT9224 four-byte CPU tag from mtk_ppe_offload1

x-wrt's natflow support patch (995-0001-hwnat-add-natflow-flow-offload-
support) switches the MediaTek ethernet driver to its own mtk_ppe_offload1.o,
so JiaY-shi's YT9224 four-byte port-tag support (967-41, which patches
mtk_ppe_offload.c) never reaches the build on x-wrt.

On GL-BE14000 the LAN ports lan1-4 and sfp hang off a YT9224 running in
yt922x_4b tag mode on eth1.  Every hardware-offloaded flow whose egress is one
of those ports - both directions of LAN<->LAN and WAN->LAN downloads - is
programmed with mtk_foe_entry_set_dsa(), which emits the MediaTek private CPU
tag (l2->etype = BIT(port), i.e. the bytes "00 <portmask> 00 00").  The YT9224
expects an 802.1Q shaped tag ("81 00" + yt922x_4b_port_tag()), cannot resolve
the destination port and drops or misroutes the frames.  The PPE entry still
binds with the correct port bits, so the breakage is silent: throughput
collapses and TCP retransmits explode.

Measured on GL-BE14000 with natflow at its shipped default
(ifname_group_type=0) and a 2.5 Gbit/s LAN client:
  hwnat=0 -> 2.34 Gbit/s (software fast path, correct)
  hwnat=1 -> 0.09-0.15 Gbit/s, ~6x wire amplification from retransmits

Feed the port ctrl through the VLAN TCI instead, mirroring 967-41.

Signed-off-by: WorkBuddy <noreply@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload1.c	2026-09-15 12:45:02.623082606 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload1.c	2026-09-15 12:45:02.623705441 +0000
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <net/pkt_cls.h>
 #include <net/dsa.h>
 #include <linux/dsa/8021q.h>
+#include <linux/dsa/yt922x.h>
 #include "mtk_eth_soc.h"
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED
 #include "mtk_wed.h"
@@ -343,6 +344,19 @@
 		}
 		if ((dest->dsa_port & 0xff00)) {
 			mtk_foe_entry_set_vlan(eth, entry, dest->dsa_port >> 4);
+		} else if (dest->dev->dsa_ptr &&
+		           dest->dev->dsa_ptr->tag_ops->proto == DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_4B) {
+			/* The YT9224 four-byte CPU tag is 802.1Q shaped:
+			 * 0x8100 + yt922x_4b_port_tag().  The MediaTek private
+			 * tag produced by mtk_foe_entry_set_dsa() (BIT(port)
+			 * in the etype field) cannot be decoded by that
+			 * switch, so push the port ctrl through the VLAN TCI.
+			 */
+			u16 ctrl = yt922x_4b_port_tag(dest->dsa_port);
+
+			if (!ctrl)
+				return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+			mtk_foe_entry_set_vlan(eth, entry, ctrl);
 		} else {
 			mtk_foe_entry_set_dsa(eth, entry, dest->dsa_port);
 		}
@@ -472,6 +486,19 @@
 		}
 		if ((dest->dsa_port & 0xff00)) {
 			mtk_foe_entry_set_vlan(eth, entry, dest->dsa_port >> 4);
+		} else if (dest->dev->dsa_ptr &&
+		           dest->dev->dsa_ptr->tag_ops->proto == DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_4B) {
+			/* The YT9224 four-byte CPU tag is 802.1Q shaped:
+			 * 0x8100 + yt922x_4b_port_tag().  The MediaTek private
+			 * tag produced by mtk_foe_entry_set_dsa() (BIT(port)
+			 * in the etype field) cannot be decoded by that
+			 * switch, so push the port ctrl through the VLAN TCI.
+			 */
+			u16 ctrl = yt922x_4b_port_tag(dest->dsa_port);
+
+			if (!ctrl)
+				return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+			mtk_foe_entry_set_vlan(eth, entry, ctrl);
 		} else {
 			mtk_foe_entry_set_dsa(eth, entry, dest->dsa_port);
 		}
